-- title:
--   Special fibre of the blow-up chart is the Drinfeld curve
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$ and a natural number $M' \neq 0$ with $q \nmid M'$, and a prime $\ell$ with $\ell \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell \mid M'$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero, $\zeta \in L$ a primitive $q$-th root of unity, and assume (hypothesis `hι`) that there is a ring homomorphism $L \to \mathbb{C}$ carrying $\zeta$ to $\exp(2\pi i/q)$. Let $H_1 \le (\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times$ be the intersection of [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH q M'`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelJacobian.html#L22) — the kernel of the reduction of unit groups `ZMod.unitsMap` along the divisibility `dvd_sq_mul q M'` — with the kernel of reduction to $(\mathbb{Z}/\ell)^\times$ (via $\ell \mid q^2 M'$), and let $K$ be the intermediate field of $L((t))$ over $L$ given by [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.xHFunctionField (q^2*M') H₁)`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), i.e. the subfield generated over $L$ by the coefficientwise image under [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81) of the function field of $X_{H_1}(q^2M')$ inside $\mathbb{Q}((t))$.
--
--   Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain, Henselian local, with algebraically closed residue field, equipped with an $A$-algebra structure on $L$ making $L$ the fraction field of $A$, such that $q \in \mathfrak{m}_A$ and $\zeta$ lies in the image of $A$; let $K$ carry an $A$-algebra structure compatible with that of $L$. Let $j \in K$ be nonzero with image in $L((t))$ equal to [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81), the coefficientwise base change of the $q$-expansion $\mathsf{q}^{-1}\cdot\mathrm{jNumQ}$ of the modular invariant. Let $\varpi$ be a uniformiser of $A$ ($\mathfrak{m}_A = (\varpi)$) and let $\varpi_t \in A$ satisfy $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1} = q\,u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$.
--
--   Write $C :=$ `chartAlgFin A K j`, the $A$-subalgebra `chartAlg A K {j}` of $K$ attached to the singleton $\{j\}$, and $X :=$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236), the pushout scheme of the two chart maps, with structure morphism `toBase` to $\operatorname{Spec} A$.
--
--   Supersingular point data: $y \subseteq C$ is a maximal ideal containing the image of $\varpi$, and the hypothesis `hss` requires that for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi : C \to \Omega$ with kernel $y$, the element $\varphi(\mathrm{jChartFin})$ (the image of $j$) lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), that is: every elliptic curve over $\Omega$ whose $j$-invariant is that element has no nonzero point killed by $q$.
--
--   Point on the model: $z$ is a point of $X$; $\varpi_z$ is the element of the stalk of $X$ at $z$ obtained as the germ at $z$ of the image of $\varpi$ under `toBase` (hypothesis `hϖz`), and `hz` requires $\varpi_z$ to lie in the maximal ideal of that stalk. Further, $y'$ is a point of `XFin` $= \operatorname{Spec} C$ with `ιFin`$(y') = z$, the hypothesis `hss'` repeats the supersingularity condition above for ring homomorphisms out of $C$ with kernel $y'.\mathrm{asIdeal}$, and `hy'y` requires $y'.\mathrm{asIdeal} = y$.
--
--   Local model data: $W_1$ is a discrete valuation domain, complete for the adic topology of its maximal ideal, $\sigma_1 : A \to W_1$ a ring homomorphism with $\mathfrak{m}_{W_1} = (\sigma_1 \varpi)$; $f_1, u_1, v_1 \in W_1[[X_0,X_1]]$ with $u_1, v_1$ units and
--   $$f_1 \equiv \mathrm{drinfeldForm}_q = X_0X_1^q - X_0^qX_1 \pmod{(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}};$$
--   and $e_1$ is a ring isomorphism from the adic completion of the stalk of $X$ at $z$ with respect to its maximal ideal onto
--   $$S := W_1[[X_0,X_1]]\big/\big(C(\sigma_1(\varpi_t^{\,q+1}))\,v_1 - f_1u_1\big).$$
--
--   Blow-up data: $J$ is an ideal of $C$, and $B$ is the $A$-subalgebra of $K$ obtained by restricting scalars from the $C$-subalgebra generated by $\{x \in K : \exists i \in J,\ x\cdot\varpi_t = i\}$, so $B = C[J/\varpi_t]$, with $C \le B$ (hypothesis `hCB`).
--
--   Throughout, $\Psi : C \to S$ denotes the composite of the canonical map `germY` from $C$ to the stalk at $z$ (global sections over the open image of `ιFin`, followed by the germ at $z$), the completion map, and $e_1$; $\mathrm{mk}_S$ denotes the quotient map $W_1[[X_0,X_1]] \to S$, and $\mathfrak{n} := (\mathrm{mk}_S\,C(\sigma_1\varpi), \mathrm{mk}_S X_0, \mathrm{mk}_S X_1)$.
--
--   The hypothesis `hbridge` (nine clauses) requires: the contraction $\Psi^{-1}(\mathfrak{n})$ equals $y$; for every $n$ and every $s \in S$ there is $a \in C$ with $\Psi(a) - s \in \mathfrak{n}^n$ (density); $\Psi(a) = \mathrm{mk}_S(C(\sigma_1 a))$ for all $a \in A$; every $c \in C$ is congruent modulo $y$ to the image of some $a \in A$; every $w \in W_1$ is congruent modulo $\mathfrak{m}_{W_1}$ to $\sigma_1 a$ for some $a \in A$; $\sigma_1^{-1}(\mathfrak{m}_{W_1}) = \mathfrak{m}_A$; $\mathfrak{n}$ is maximal; every maximal ideal of $S$ equals $\mathfrak{n}$; and $S$ is flat as a module over $C$ via $\Psi$.
--
--   The hypothesis `hcentre` (four clauses) requires: $\Psi(J)\,S = (\mathrm{mk}_S\,C(\sigma_1\varpi_t), \mathrm{mk}_S X_0, \mathrm{mk}_S X_1)$; there is an ideal $I$ of $C$ with $J = \Psi^{-1}\big((\mathrm{mk}_S\,C(\sigma_1\varpi_t), \mathrm{mk}_S X_0, \mathrm{mk}_S X_1)\big) \cap I$ and $I + y = C$; $J \le y$; and the image of $\varpi_t$ in $C$ lies in $J$. Finally, an algebra structure of $\mathrm{GaloisField}(q,2) = \mathbb{F}_{q^2}$ on the residue field of $A$ is given.
--
--   Conclusion. Put $L_{\mathrm{loc}} :=$ `Localization.Away` at $\mathrm{mk}_S(C(\sigma_1\varpi_t))$, with structure map $\iota_S : S \to L_{\mathrm{loc}}$, and
--   $$x_0 := \iota_S(\mathrm{mk}_S X_0)\cdot \mathrm{invSelf},\qquad x_1 := \iota_S(\mathrm{mk}_S X_1)\cdot\mathrm{invSelf},$$
--   where $\mathrm{invSelf}$ is the inverse of $\mathrm{mk}_S(C(\sigma_1\varpi_t))$ in the localisation, and let $R_{\mathrm{loc}}$ be the subring of $L_{\mathrm{loc}}$ generated by the range of $\iota_S$ together with $x_0, x_1$. Then there exist a ring homomorphism $\Phi : B \to L_{\mathrm{loc}}$, membership witnesses $\iota_S(s) \in R_{\mathrm{loc}}$ for all $s \in S$, $x_0 \in R_{\mathrm{loc}}$, $x_1 \in R_{\mathrm{loc}}$ and $\Phi(b) \in R_{\mathrm{loc}}$ for all $b \in B$, a ring homomorphism $t_W : W_1 \to \kappa_A$ to the residue field of $A$, an element $c_R \in \kappa_A$, and ring homomorphisms $\rho_R : R_{\mathrm{loc}} \to \mathrm{CoordRing}_q(\kappa_A)$ and $\rho : B \to \mathrm{CoordRing}_q(\kappa_A)$ into the Drinfeld coordinate ring $\kappa_A[X_0,X_1]/\mathrm{drinfeldIdeal}_q$, such that:
--
--   (i) $\Phi$ extends $\Psi$: for every $a \in C$, $\Phi(a) = \iota_S(\Psi(a))$ (the element of $B$ being the image of $a$ under `hCB`);
--
--   (ii) $\Phi$ divides by $\varpi_t$ on the centre: for $x \in B$ and $i \in J \subseteq C$ with $x\cdot\varpi_t = i$ in $K$, one has $\Phi(x)\cdot\iota_S(\mathrm{mk}_S(C(\sigma_1\varpi_t))) = \iota_S(\Psi(i))$;
--
--   (iii) $t_W \circ \sigma_1$ is the residue map of $A$, and $t_W$ vanishes on $\mathfrak{m}_{W_1}$;
--
--   (iv) $c_R \neq 0$;
--
--   (v) for every $F \in W_1[[X_0,X_1]]$, $\rho_R(\iota_S(\mathrm{mk}_S F))$ is the image in $\mathrm{CoordRing}_q(\kappa_A)$ of $t_W$ applied to the constant coefficient of $F$;
--
--   (vi) $\rho_R(x_0) = c_R\cdot \mathrm{x}$ and $\rho_R(x_1) = c_R\cdot \mathrm{y}$, where $\mathrm{x}, \mathrm{y}$ are the classes of $X_0, X_1$ in $\mathrm{CoordRing}_q(\kappa_A)$ and $c_R$ acts through the structure map $\kappa_A \to \mathrm{CoordRing}_q(\kappa_A)$;
--
--   (vii) $\rho(b) = \rho_R(\Phi(b))$ for all $b \in B$;
--
--   (viii) $\rho$ is surjective;
--
--   (ix) for $b \in B$, $\rho(b) = 0$ if and only if $b$ lies in the ideal of $B$ generated by the image of $y$ under the inclusion $C \le B$;
--
--   (x) $\rho(\mathrm{algebraMap}_A(a))$ is the image of $\mathrm{residue}_A(a)$ in $\mathrm{CoordRing}_q(\kappa_A)$, for every $a \in A$.
--
--   This is the identification of the special fibre of the blown-up chart $B = C[J/\varpi_t]$ at a supersingular point of the integral model of $X_{H_1}(q^2M')$ with the affine Drinfeld curve $X_0X_1^q - X_0^qX_1 = \text{const}$ over the residue field of $A$, obtained by transporting the local blow-up chart $R_{\mathrm{loc}} = S[X_0/\varpi_t, X_1/\varpi_t]$ through the completion isomorphism $e_1$; the surjection $\rho$ with kernel the ideal generated by $y$ exhibits $B/yB \cong \mathrm{CoordRing}_q(\kappa_A)$ compatibly with the residue map of $A$. It feeds the analysis of the Galois action (decomposition and inertia) on the Drinfeld fibre of the blow-up chart and the computation of tangent coordinates on the completed stalk, in the auxiliary-level $\Gamma_1(\ell)$ frame used for small $q$.
